  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The remainder \\(R\\) obtained by dividing \\(x^{100}\\) by \\(x^2-3x+2\\) is a polynomial of degree less than \\(2.\\) Then \\(R\\) may be written as:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2^{100}-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2^{100}(x-1)-(x-2)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2^{100}(x-3)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x(2^{100}-1)+2(2^{99}-1)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2^{100}(x+1)-(x+2)\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1969-p34.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Write \\(R(x)=ax+b.\\) Since the divisor is \\((x-1)(x-2),\\) evaluating the division identity at its roots gives \\[ R(1)=1,\\qquad R(2)=2^{100}. \\] Therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} R(x)&=1+(2^{100}-1)(x-1)\\\\ &=2^{100}(x-1)-(x-2). \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(R(x)=ax+b\\) and use \\(x^2-3x+2=(x-1)(x-2)\\)",
        "Evaluate the division identity at \\(x=1\\) and \\(x=2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
